# Build-time configuration for the production static export.
#
# NOT A SECRET FILE. Everything here is compiled into the JavaScript the browser
# downloads — that is what the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix means. Do not put anything here
# that you would not print on the homepage.

# Web3Forms access key for the inquiry form, the document-request form and the
# newsletter form.
#
# WHY IT IS IN THE REPOSITORY AND NOT A SECRET STORE:
#
# Web3Forms keys are public by design — the key has to appear in the page's own
# JavaScript for a static site to post to the API at all, so hiding it in a secret
# store buys nothing and costs the one thing that matters here: a build that forgets
# it. The form is built by whoever holds the release baton, on their own machine,
# and there is no CI step that could inject a secret into that build. From launch
# until 2026-09-21 this variable was never set, so EVERY "send" the site ever
# received failed — a Brazilian buyer on 09-16 wrote a full specification and
# pressed send three times; a Spanish buyer on 09-18 spent 17:56 on /es/contact/
# and submitted at 14:23 into nothing. That is what a secret nobody can see costs.
#
# The key's only capability is "post a message to lock@cantonlock.com". It cannot
# read mail, change settings or spend money. Free tier is 250 messages a month.
#
# Issued 2026-09-21 by the client, registered to lock@cantonlock.com.
NEXT_PUBLIC_W3F_KEY=799e6316-168b-430f-acb8-a6e49cf6c2d5
